From b0f1ffd3944a95d863fb6cd6f030a6d713def1c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Wed, 18 Mar 2026 23:54:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] SurfaceFlinger: defer all display mode changes until boot is
 finished

On GSI targets with multi-rate displays (e.g. 60Hz+120Hz), the upstream
boot guard in initiateDisplayModeChanges is gated on synced_resolution_switch.
When that flag is false (its aconfig default on many vendor builds), the guard
is a no-op and mode changes reach the HWC before the display pipeline is stable.

This causes a failed DRM atomic commit on older vendor HWC implementations
(MediaTek, Qualcomm legacy blobs), leaving the CRTC in a broken state and
producing a permanently black screen despite the rest of the framework booting
successfully.

Remove the flag condition to unconditionally defer all mode changes until
mBootStage == FINISHED, regardless of aconfig flag state. DisplayManager will
re-request the preferred mode once boot completes and the pipeline is stable.
---
 services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp b/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp
index 0235bc295a..4b049a0c5a 100644
--- a/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp
+++ b/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp
@@ -1651,8 +1651,13 @@ void SurfaceFlinger::applyActiveMode(display::DisplayModeRequest&& activeMode) {
 }
 
 void SurfaceFlinger::initiateDisplayModeChanges() {
-    if (FlagManager::getInstance().synced_resolution_switch() && mBootStage != BootStage::FINISHED)
-            [[unlikely]] {
+    // [GSI] Unconditionally defer ALL display mode changes until boot is finished.
+    // The upstream guard is gated on synced_resolution_switch, but on GSI targets
+    // with older vendor HWCs (e.g. MediaTek, Qualcomm on older blobs) any mode
+    // change before the display pipeline is stable can cause a failed DRM atomic
+    // commit, leaving the CRTC broken and the screen permanently black. Block
+    // everything until mBootStage == FINISHED regardless of aconfig flags.
+    if (mBootStage != BootStage::FINISHED) [[unlikely]] {
         return;
     }
 
